(screaming)

1959
01:13:50,700 --> 01:13:52,067
- [Tom] Ah, that's my ride.

1960
01:13:52,067 --> 01:13:54,300
- Oh I'm sorry, Jondor.
- [Crow] Oh you are not.

1961
01:13:54,300 --> 01:13:56,800
- I won't be able to stay
to enjoy your last moments

1962
01:13:56,800 --> 01:14:00,433
but I am urgently
required elsewhere.

1963
01:14:00,433 --> 01:14:02,200
- [Mike] But where are the
blank checks, by the way?

1964
01:14:02,200 --> 01:14:03,733
Well, I'll find 'em.

1965
01:14:03,733 --> 01:14:06,133
- [Tom] Visit the
La Brea Tar Pits.

1966
01:14:06,133 --> 01:14:08,300
(dramatic music)

1967
01:14:08,300 --> 01:14:09,100
- Okay.

1968
01:14:09,100 --> 01:14:10,367
- [Crow] It's all right.

1969
01:14:10,367 --> 01:14:11,733
- I guess so.
- We better keep moving then.

1970
01:14:11,733 --> 01:14:13,500
We'll never find the
boys just sitting here.

1971
01:14:13,500 --> 01:14:15,533
- May I say it just
once more, please.

1972
01:14:15,533 --> 01:14:16,367
- What?

1973
01:14:16,367 --> 01:14:17,200
- [Tom] Member.

1974
01:14:17,200 --> 01:14:18,767
- I'm scared.

1975
01:14:18,767 --> 01:14:20,767
- Well if it makes you
feel any better, so am I.

1976
01:14:20,767 --> 01:14:22,533
But we've got to go on.

1977
01:14:24,367 --> 01:14:26,700
- [Tom] Just tuck the
bone back under the skin.

1978
01:14:28,600 --> 01:14:29,833
- Let's go.

1979
01:14:29,833 --> 01:14:30,767
- [Mike] Seems like
you need a pants horn

1980
01:14:30,767 --> 01:14:32,500
to get into those things.

1981
01:14:35,367 --> 01:14:37,400
(screaming)

1982
01:14:37,400 --> 01:14:38,467
- Ah, ah, ah!

1983
01:14:40,133 --> 01:14:41,133
- [Crow] Choo!

1984
01:14:41,133 --> 01:14:42,300
(girls screaming)

1985
01:14:42,300 --> 01:14:43,300
- That's Betty.
- And Jeanne.

1986
01:14:43,300 --> 01:14:44,300
- Come on.

1987
01:14:44,300 --> 01:14:45,133
- [Tom] And weird guy.

1988
01:14:46,300 --> 01:14:49,267
- [Mike] Uh, let me
baptize you just once.

1989
01:14:51,933 --> 01:14:53,567
(girls screaming)

1990
01:14:53,567 --> 01:14:55,300
- [Crow] How about
next Wednesday then?

1991
01:14:56,800 --> 01:14:59,033
- [Mike] This guy always
sits next to me on the bus.

1992
01:14:59,033 --> 01:15:01,200
(man screaming)

1993
01:15:01,200 --> 01:15:04,067
- [Tom] It amuses me that
someone is chewing the scenery.

1994
01:15:05,867 --> 01:15:08,433
(man shouting)

1995
01:15:11,333 --> 01:15:13,100
- [Crow] Your island
is really very, oh!

1996
01:15:13,100 --> 01:15:15,100
- [Tom] He culls the
weak from the herd.

1997
01:15:17,067 --> 01:15:18,833
Robert Reed is Buford T. Pusser.

1998
01:15:18,833 --> 01:15:20,233
- [Crow] In Prancing Tall.

1999
01:15:21,900 --> 01:15:23,133
- Are you all right?

2000
01:15:23,133 --> 01:15:24,600
- [Mike] Have we had
the clam bake yet?

2001
01:15:24,600 --> 01:15:27,000
- Come on, let's
get outta here fast.

2002
01:15:27,000 --> 01:15:28,500
- [Tom] I wish they'd
invent computers

2003
01:15:28,500 --> 01:15:30,100
so I'd have somewhere to belong.

2004
01:15:31,967 --> 01:15:34,000
- [Crow] Well this
movie's back on track.

2005
01:15:38,267 --> 01:15:40,533
(groaning)

2006
01:15:43,267 --> 01:15:45,000
- [Tom] Well, back at it.

2007
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:46,900
I think it's the
others who are crazy.

2008
01:15:48,100 --> 01:15:50,567
- [Crow] Oh I blew it. I
should've said, ew, eh.

2009
01:15:50,567 --> 01:15:52,000
Ew instead of eh.

2010
01:15:52,000 --> 01:15:52,967
- So it's you.

2011
01:15:54,433 --> 01:15:56,167
- [Mike] You're looking well.

2012
01:15:56,167 --> 01:15:57,900
- I had thought to permit you

2013
01:15:57,900 --> 01:16:00,667
to enjoy the
hospitality of my island

2014
01:16:00,667 --> 01:16:02,300
while I took care of
more pressing business.

2015
01:16:02,300 --> 01:16:04,467
- [Tom] Can I get a
grunt in here edgewise?

2016
01:16:06,767 --> 01:16:07,733
- [Crow] I'd rather
die than have to listen

2017
01:16:07,733 --> 01:16:09,033
to that guy talk.

2018
01:16:09,033 --> 01:16:11,400
(man screaming)

2019
01:16:11,400 --> 01:16:12,800
- [Mike] It kinda hurts.

2020
01:16:13,733 --> 01:16:16,467
(dramatic music)

2021
01:16:20,567 --> 01:16:21,933
- [Tom] Ah, so it's you.

2022
01:16:27,400 --> 01:16:29,067
- [Crow] Reduce, recycle, reuse.

2023
01:16:30,900 --> 01:16:33,033
- [Mike] You know, older men
always carry handkerchiefs.

2024
01:16:33,033 --> 01:16:34,267
- [Tom] And this is why.

2025
01:16:36,600 --> 01:16:38,733
- [Crow] I'm kind of
anal about this stuff.

2026
01:16:41,367 --> 01:16:44,233
- [Mike] Okay, call me if
there's any pain or discomfort.

2027
01:16:45,433 --> 01:16:47,500
- [Tom] Been good
talking to ya, so long.

2028
01:16:49,333 --> 01:16:50,800
- [Crow] You know
he may be in danger

2029
01:16:50,800 --> 01:16:53,700
of over harvesting the
game on this island.

2030
01:16:55,267 --> 01:16:56,533
- [Mike] I think
they're letting us in

2031
01:16:56,533 --> 01:16:58,000
on details we really
don't need to know.

2032
01:17:01,133 --> 01:17:03,000
- [Tom] The Kraut
is a lonely hunter.

2033
01:17:06,900 --> 01:17:09,033
- [Crow] I should just
put in some strip malls

2034
01:17:09,033 --> 01:17:10,700
and be done with it.

2035
01:17:12,100 --> 01:17:14,767
- [Mike] Really not a
lot to do on this island.

2036
01:17:14,767 --> 01:17:17,533
(dramatic music)

2037
01:17:21,500 --> 01:17:24,533
- [Crow] Looks like a
really uncomfortable crotch.

2038
01:17:24,533 --> 01:17:25,467
- I don't know how
long we can hold onto

2039
01:17:25,467 --> 01:17:27,100
this kind of luck.

2040
01:17:27,100 --> 01:17:29,867
- If Balleau doesn't
get us the strain will.

2041
01:17:29,867 --> 01:17:32,267
- We're gonna have to try
a real grand stand play.

2042
01:17:32,267 --> 01:17:34,433
(humming)

2043
01:17:36,100 --> 01:17:37,333
- From the sound they made,

2044
01:17:37,333 --> 01:17:38,633
I'd say the whole bunch
is out looking for us.

2045
01:17:38,633 --> 01:17:40,833
- Good, at least they'll
be outta the house.

2046
01:17:42,267 --> 01:17:43,500
- Pete drop down and see if
you can see any signs of him.

2047
01:17:43,500 --> 01:17:44,500
- [Crow] Well why
don't you drop down

2048
01:17:44,500 --> 01:17:46,400
and kiss my pink behind, well.

2049
01:17:46,400 --> 01:17:47,833
- Be careful.

2050
01:17:47,833 --> 01:17:50,333
- [Crow] I want you the be
alive when I break up with you.

2051
01:17:51,200 --> 01:17:52,433
- Let me at 'em.

2052
01:17:52,433 --> 01:17:54,233
- [Tom] Damn the
torpedoes, please.

2053
01:17:55,600 --> 01:17:56,767
- [Crow] Okay, dropping down

2054
01:17:56,767 --> 01:17:58,800
oh, oh, I could hurt my ankle.

2055
01:17:58,800 --> 01:18:01,200
I just have to drop and then.

2056
01:18:02,933 --> 01:18:04,900
- It's okay, it's okay, come on.

2057
01:18:04,900 --> 01:18:06,767
- [Crow] He's a
regular Sacagawea.

2058
01:18:08,467 --> 01:18:09,800
- [Tom] I jumped
down and scouted

2059
01:18:09,800 --> 01:18:11,833
the place out like
you said, I did!

2060
01:18:16,433 --> 01:18:18,100
- Look, we haven't got
a chance without a gun.

2061
01:18:18,100 --> 01:18:19,833
We've got to get back
into the trophy room.

2062
01:18:19,833 --> 01:18:21,500
- We can't, we just
got outta there.

2063
01:18:21,500 --> 01:18:23,867
- That's just why we can take
a chance on going back there.

2064
01:18:23,867 --> 01:18:25,633
Balleau's guards will still
be out looking for you girls.

2065
01:18:25,633 --> 01:18:27,533
Now if we can shake Balleau

2066
01:18:27,533 --> 01:18:29,533
and get back there
before the guards do,

2067
01:18:29,533 --> 01:18:32,533
we can get the guns and maybe
have a chance to stay alive

2068
01:18:32,533 --> 01:18:35,000
long enough to find
the boat, come on.

2069
01:18:35,000 --> 01:18:36,400
- [Mike] You see
me scouting, honey?

2070
01:18:36,400 --> 01:18:37,233
I scouted.

2071
01:18:38,100 --> 01:18:39,600
(light music)

2072
01:18:39,600 --> 01:18:42,900
- [Crow] I haven't seen a
coworker for weeks, oh well.

2073
01:18:42,900 --> 01:18:45,967
- [Tom] I will not
let down my vigil.

2074
01:18:47,533 --> 01:18:50,300
- That's one guy that's not
out combing the bushes for us.

2075
01:18:50,300 --> 01:18:51,500
- Should we jump him, Johnny?

2076
01:18:51,500 --> 01:18:53,233
- No, I don't think so.

2077
01:18:53,233 --> 01:18:54,167
I think our best chance

2078
01:18:54,167 --> 01:18:56,467
is to try and sneak past him.

2079
01:18:58,200 --> 01:19:01,167
- [Crow] I gots one job
but I does it well, arr.

2080
01:19:02,700 --> 01:19:04,800
And I hates Robert Reed.

2081
01:19:07,567 --> 01:19:09,433
- [Tom] Hey mister,
can we go in now?

2082
01:19:10,500 --> 01:19:12,767
(giggling)

2083
01:19:16,733 --> 01:19:17,967
- [Crow] Maybe I
can kill a bush.

2084
01:19:17,967 --> 01:19:19,733
Ah, it wouldn't be the same.

2085
01:19:21,267 --> 01:19:22,633
- [Tom] I suppose I
shoulda kept my town house

2086
01:19:22,633 --> 01:19:24,000
in Manhattan, well.

2087
01:19:25,533 --> 01:19:27,200
- [Mike] Ah, time for my story.

2088
01:19:28,933 --> 01:19:30,400
- [Crow] I wonder if there's any

2089
01:19:30,400 --> 01:19:32,300
of that German potato
salad left in the fridge.

2090
01:19:35,233 --> 01:19:39,633
♪ Deutschland,
Deutschland, uber alles♪

2091
01:19:39,633 --> 01:19:42,400
(dramatic music)

2092
01:19:43,933 --> 01:19:45,733
- [Mike] It's just
as I remember it.

2093
01:19:47,900 --> 01:19:48,867
- [Crow] Are you
guys ready for this?

2094
01:19:48,867 --> 01:19:50,233
Remote control everything.

2095
01:19:53,700 --> 01:19:54,533
- It's locked.

2096
01:19:54,533 --> 01:19:55,367
- Are you surprised?

2097
01:19:55,367 --> 01:19:56,900
- Oh very funny.

2098
01:19:56,900 --> 01:19:58,067
Don't just stand there.

2099
01:19:58,067 --> 01:19:59,533
Try and find something
to open it with.

2100
01:19:59,533 --> 01:20:00,867
- [Tom] This would be the kind
of blood hunt I get in on.

2101
01:20:02,800 --> 01:20:04,067
- Well if we get it,
what are we gonna do?

2102
01:20:04,067 --> 01:20:05,433
- We're gonna try
and get outta here

2103
01:20:05,433 --> 01:20:06,333
and find the boat.

2104
01:20:06,333 --> 01:20:07,833
- Oh thank goodness.

2105
01:20:07,833 --> 01:20:09,933
I don't wanna stay in here
any longer than we have to.

2106
01:20:09,933 --> 01:20:11,500
- Yeah, yeah, that
oughta do the trick.

2107
01:20:11,500 --> 01:20:12,500
- [Tom] That was almost as hard

2108
01:20:12,500 --> 01:20:13,967
as the time that
I went scouting.

2109
01:20:13,967 --> 01:20:14,800
- [Crow] Shut up.

2110
01:20:17,100 --> 01:20:19,600
(light music)

2111
01:20:23,467 --> 01:20:27,733
Get all the way out there
and my laxative kicks in.

2112
01:20:28,933 --> 01:20:30,200
- [Tom] All quiet sir.

2113
01:20:31,833 --> 01:20:33,367
- Neck broke.

2114
01:20:33,367 --> 01:20:34,867
- [Mike] You get what
you pay for, I guess.

2115
01:20:34,867 --> 01:20:36,500
- [Crow] No wait, I think I have

2116
01:20:36,500 --> 01:20:38,933
a neck in here
somewhere, ah yes.

2117
01:20:40,500 --> 01:20:42,833
- [Mike] Had a great job
as an actuary downtown

2118
01:20:42,833 --> 01:20:44,867
but no, gotta come
out and buy an island.

2119
01:20:45,833 --> 01:20:48,633
(dramatic music)

2120
01:20:52,400 --> 01:20:57,200
- [Tom] Well look at this
Lucas McCain's armoire.

2121
01:20:57,200 --> 01:20:59,000
- [Crow] I'm the NRA.

2122
01:20:59,000 --> 01:21:00,600
- There's no ammo here.

2123
01:21:00,600 --> 01:21:02,200
- Well there's gotta be.

2124
01:21:02,200 --> 01:21:03,833
These guns are useless
to us without it.

2125
01:21:03,833 --> 01:21:05,000
- I know, I know.

2126
01:21:05,000 --> 01:21:05,833
- Somebody's coming.

2127
01:21:05,833 --> 01:21:07,200
- Let's get outta here.

2128
01:21:07,200 --> 01:21:09,433
- [Mike] "Scooby Doo"
the motion picture.

2129
01:21:10,533 --> 01:21:12,600
- [Tom] Shh, I
can't stop laughing.

2130
01:21:13,433 --> 01:21:15,333
(cackling)

2131
01:21:15,333 --> 01:21:17,300
- [Crow] He should be thankful
for his smoking jacket

2132
01:21:17,300 --> 01:21:19,700
or else he'd be walking
around in his underwear.

2133
01:21:21,633 --> 01:21:24,600
- [Mike] I think I'll settle
in with some erma Bombay.

2134
01:21:24,600 --> 01:21:26,900
- [Tom] Maybe a little
schnitzel bonk for dinner.

2135
01:21:26,900 --> 01:21:28,867
- [Crow] I hope I
didn't kill the cook.

2136
01:21:33,933 --> 01:21:36,467
(ominous music)
- [Mike] This guy looks like

2137
01:21:36,467 --> 01:21:37,733
a sockeye salmon about to spawn.

2138
01:21:39,767 --> 01:21:42,000
- [Tom] Ack, those
darn Mendez boys.

2139
01:21:44,767 --> 01:21:46,933
- [Crow] Oh good, my
lingerie is still here.

2140
01:21:48,733 --> 01:21:50,100
- [Mike] I feel so violated.

2141
01:21:53,300 --> 01:21:54,100
- [Tom] Manos.

2142
01:21:55,467 --> 01:21:57,300
- [Crow] I wish the bear
would put on some pants.

2143
01:21:58,500 --> 01:22:01,133
- [Tom] No cookies, not
now, not ever, never!

2144
01:22:01,133 --> 01:22:03,633
(light music)

2145
01:22:07,633 --> 01:22:10,800
- [Tom] You know, I
could sublet this.

2146
01:22:12,467 --> 01:22:15,500
- [Mike] Maybe I do have
room for a pool table.

2147
01:22:17,600 --> 01:22:21,600
♪ But a cave is not a home♪

2148
01:22:21,600 --> 01:22:24,267
- [Crow] This is the biggest
bathroom I've ever seen.

2149
01:22:27,167 --> 01:22:30,200
- [Mike] Ladies and
gentlemen, Spalding Gray.

2150
01:22:30,200 --> 01:22:32,733
- [Balleau] Well
then, I'm flattered

2151
01:22:32,733 --> 01:22:33,967
that someone should
want to further look

2152
01:22:33,967 --> 01:22:35,200
at my little souvenirs.

2153
01:22:36,733 --> 01:22:38,900
No one else has ever
come back a second time.

2154
01:22:38,900 --> 01:22:40,967
- [Tom] Maybe I'm over charging.

2155
01:22:40,967 --> 01:22:42,900
- [Balleau] Alive.

2156
01:22:42,900 --> 01:22:44,400
- [Mike] Hello?

2157
01:22:44,400 --> 01:22:45,733
- It's rather dark in here.

2158
01:22:47,133 --> 01:22:49,367
Perhaps we should have
a little more light.

2159
01:22:49,367 --> 01:22:50,367
- [Crow] Clap on.

2160
01:22:52,533 --> 01:22:53,333
Mammy, sir.

2161
01:22:54,900 --> 01:22:56,100
- Well, let's try else where.

2162
01:22:56,100 --> 01:22:57,867
- [Tom] He's regained
his sang foud.

2163
01:22:59,800 --> 01:23:01,400
- Or there.

2164
01:23:01,400 --> 01:23:03,400
- [Crow] Does he even take
'em out and play with 'em?

2165
01:23:03,400 --> 01:23:04,900
- Well, well.

2166
01:23:04,900 --> 01:23:06,700
- [Mike] Just switch 'em on
all at once you show off.

2167
01:23:08,800 --> 01:23:10,000
- Or there I imagine.

2168
01:23:10,000 --> 01:23:11,833
- [Tom] Yes, I call
that one Lutheran Love.

2169
01:23:14,300 --> 01:23:16,333
- There's plenty of time.

2170
01:23:16,333 --> 01:23:17,667
- [Crow] I've got fudge.

2171
01:23:19,533 --> 01:23:21,333
- It's strange about
these old walls.

2172
01:23:21,333 --> 01:23:22,567
- [Tom] Yeah, what's that?

2173
01:23:22,567 --> 01:23:25,900
- The smallest
sound is amplified.

2174
01:23:25,900 --> 01:23:28,100
If one sits quite
still one can hear

2175
01:23:28,100 --> 01:23:29,900
the slightest murmur.

2176
01:23:29,900 --> 01:23:30,833
- [Tom] Murmur.

2177
01:23:30,833 --> 01:23:32,067
- [Mike] Murmur, murmur, murmur.

2178
01:23:32,067 --> 01:23:33,500
- Sometimes even the
slightest breath.

2179
01:23:33,500 --> 01:23:35,200
- [Crow] Really?

2180
01:23:35,200 --> 01:23:36,433
- [Tom] See, I'm suggesting

2181
01:23:36,433 --> 01:23:37,633
that there may be
someone in here.

2182
01:23:37,633 --> 01:23:39,400
- A certain closeness
about this place.

2183
01:23:40,667 --> 01:23:42,533
I've never corrected it.

2184
01:23:42,533 --> 01:23:44,533
It helps preserve my trophies.

2185
01:23:44,533 --> 01:23:46,000
- [Mike] Maybe when I retire.

2186
01:23:46,000 --> 01:23:48,467
- But at times it does
make breathing difficult.

2187
01:23:48,467 --> 01:23:49,733
- [Crow] He does
this twice a day

2188
01:23:49,733 --> 01:23:51,567
and once in awhile he
actually finds somebody.

2189
01:23:51,567 --> 01:23:55,433
- I've sat here so long that
I find I can sit for hours

2190
01:23:55,433 --> 01:23:58,000
and not make a single sound.

2191
01:23:58,000 --> 01:23:59,667
- [Mike] Why don't
you demonstrate?

2192
01:23:59,667 --> 01:24:00,667
(chortle)

2193
01:24:00,667 --> 01:24:02,767
- Not a single sound.

2194
01:24:02,767 --> 01:24:04,400
(coughing)

2195
01:24:04,400 --> 01:24:06,200
- [Tom] I got you, I
got you, I got you!

2196
01:24:06,200 --> 01:24:08,100
- A single sound.

2197
01:24:08,100 --> 01:24:09,533
- [Mike] Not a single sound.

2198
01:24:09,533 --> 01:24:10,500
- [Tom] Single sound.

2199
01:24:10,500 --> 01:24:12,300
- Stay just where you are.

2200
01:24:12,300 --> 01:24:14,800
- [Crow] You guys are
pathetic, look at you.

2201
01:24:14,800 --> 01:24:17,300
- That's far enough fellow,
don't come any closer.

2202
01:24:18,733 --> 01:24:19,933
- I think it was rather rude

2203
01:24:19,933 --> 01:24:22,300
of you to force
open my gun cabinet.

2204
01:24:22,300 --> 01:24:26,367
But I'll overlook it since you
spared my ammunition chest.

2205
01:24:26,367 --> 01:24:27,667
- [Mike] Pete, Pete, poker face.

2206
01:24:27,667 --> 01:24:30,500
- Oh yes, I know your
guns are quite useless.

2207
01:24:31,933 --> 01:24:32,767
No, no.

2208
01:24:32,767 --> 01:24:33,967
- [Tom] Fix bayonets!

2209
01:24:33,967 --> 01:24:35,200
- I wouldn't try
that if I were you.

2210
01:24:35,200 --> 01:24:36,300
- It would only
hasten your death

2211
01:24:36,300 --> 01:24:38,000
and that of all of your friends.

2212
01:24:38,833 --> 01:24:40,167
- Okay, Balleau.

2213
01:24:41,367 --> 01:24:42,200
You win.

2214
01:24:43,333 --> 01:24:46,600
- I never doubted it, did you?

2215
01:24:46,600 --> 01:24:48,067
- Well, why don't
you get it over with?

2216
01:24:48,067 --> 01:24:50,033
- Oh, not so fast
my young friend.

2217
01:24:51,300 --> 01:24:53,333
I have an idea
that appeals to me.

2218
01:24:53,333 --> 01:24:54,533
- [Crow] Chic peas.

2219
01:24:54,533 --> 01:24:56,600
- Let me group you
in this setting alive

2220
01:24:56,600 --> 01:24:58,933
as you will be in
death, for all time.

2221
01:24:58,933 --> 01:25:00,167
- [Mike] Well, okay.

2222
01:25:00,167 --> 01:25:01,633
- What do you mean?

2223
01:25:01,633 --> 01:25:03,400
- I'll show you, my dear.

2224
01:25:03,400 --> 01:25:04,767
I've never had the pleasure

2225
01:25:04,767 --> 01:25:06,833
of a trial arrangement
of my trophies.

2226
01:25:09,233 --> 01:25:11,733
You, Pete, over there.

2227
01:25:11,733 --> 01:25:13,700
- [Tom] Link, Julie, over there.

2228
01:25:13,700 --> 01:25:15,167
- Move!

2229
01:25:15,167 --> 01:25:16,700
- [Crow] Look over your
shoulder and wet your lips.

2230
01:25:16,700 --> 01:25:19,533
- And you my dear, I think
you'd look most effective

2231
01:25:19,533 --> 01:25:21,700
with your arms
around Johnny's neck.

2232
01:25:21,700 --> 01:25:22,900
- Now wait a minute.

2233
01:25:22,900 --> 01:25:24,500
You promised to
let the girls live.

2234
01:25:24,500 --> 01:25:27,033
- That's right, I did promise.

2235
01:25:27,033 --> 01:25:29,800
But since they obviously
helped you kill the guard

2236
01:25:29,800 --> 01:25:31,467
I'm afraid I can no
longer trust them.

2237
01:25:31,467 --> 01:25:34,700
- Guard, we didn't
kill any guard.

2238
01:25:34,700 --> 01:25:36,700
- [Mike] We didn't
steal no bike, neither.

2239
01:25:36,700 --> 01:25:39,733
- Honest, the only guard
we saw was at the gate

2240
01:25:39,733 --> 01:25:41,633
and we sneaked past him.

2241
01:25:41,633 --> 01:25:42,567
- [Crow] Snuck.

2242
01:25:42,567 --> 01:25:44,400
- Quiet, don't make a sound.

2243
01:25:44,400 --> 01:25:45,833
Any of you, not a sound.

2244
01:25:49,133 --> 01:25:52,933
- [Tom] Shoulda had a tech
rehearsal, I had to, ah.

2245
01:25:52,933 --> 01:25:54,900
- You, over to my chair.

2246
01:25:54,900 --> 01:25:56,200
And throw the last switch.

2247
01:25:57,267 --> 01:25:58,500
Move, quickly, quickly.

2248
01:25:58,500 --> 01:25:59,967
- [Mike] Finally
Pete's the AV geek

2249
01:25:59,967 --> 01:26:01,200
he's always wanted to be.

2250
01:26:03,267 --> 01:26:04,600
- [Balleau] Hurry,
the last switch.

2251
01:26:04,600 --> 01:26:06,133
- [Crow] Um, is that
the red one, sir?

2252
01:26:06,133 --> 01:26:07,067
There are two here.

2253
01:26:07,067 --> 01:26:08,533
Which one is the last one?

2254
01:26:09,700 --> 01:26:10,600
- [Tom] Huh, David Letterman.

2255
01:26:10,600 --> 01:26:11,433
- [Crow] Hey.

2256
01:26:13,967 --> 01:26:17,100
- [Mike] You got any salt, I
got a couple of hangers here.

2257
01:26:17,100 --> 01:26:18,267
- Jondor, stop.

2258
01:26:18,267 --> 01:26:19,233
- [Crow] No leeches
in the house.

2259
01:26:21,700 --> 01:26:23,200
- I warn you.

2260
01:26:23,200 --> 01:26:26,000
- [Tom] It's the blue switch,
here let me get it for you.

2261
01:26:26,967 --> 01:26:28,433
(gunshots)

2262
01:26:28,433 --> 01:26:30,600
- [Crow] Let's go hide
in the head boiling room.

2263
01:26:31,900 --> 01:26:34,800
(growling)

2264
01:26:34,800 --> 01:26:36,200
Oh, ow.

2265
01:26:36,200 --> 01:26:38,400
- [Tom] You see when lackey's
turn on their masters

2266
01:26:38,400 --> 01:26:39,367
they become bullet proof.

2267
01:26:39,367 --> 01:26:41,233
(screaming)

2268
01:26:41,233 --> 01:26:43,733
- [Crow] Hey buddy
I love ya, come on.

2269
01:26:43,733 --> 01:26:46,067
(screaming)

2270
01:26:47,567 --> 01:26:49,633
- [Crow] Yow, that hurts.

2271
01:26:51,833 --> 01:26:53,067
- [Tom] So why this symbolism?

2272
01:26:53,067 --> 01:26:55,167
Did Christ hunt people
on deserted islands?

2273
01:26:56,833 --> 01:26:58,167
- [Mike] The Johnson
coat rack company

2274
01:26:58,167 --> 01:26:59,567
issued a recall today.

2275
01:27:01,667 --> 01:27:03,500
- Take it easy Betty.

2276
01:27:03,500 --> 01:27:05,367
It's all over and
we'll be safe now.

2277
01:27:05,367 --> 01:27:06,767
- [Crow] We're free to be wry.

2278
01:27:06,767 --> 01:27:09,200
- But we're not off this
horrible island yet.

2279
01:27:09,200 --> 01:27:10,133
Those others.

2280
01:27:10,133 --> 01:27:11,333
- Don't worry about them.

2281
01:27:12,533 --> 01:27:13,767
Now that Balleau's
dead I don't think

2282
01:27:13,767 --> 01:27:15,267
that they'll give
us any trouble.

2283
01:27:15,267 --> 01:27:16,800
- [Tom] He's been so right
about everything so far.

2284
01:27:16,800 --> 01:27:18,133
- I guess Balleau
never thought he'd be

2285
01:27:18,133 --> 01:27:20,300
the prize exhibit
in his own museum.

2286
01:27:20,300 --> 01:27:21,567
- [Tom] Guess not.

2287
01:27:21,567 --> 01:27:22,733
- [Mike] You know if
earlier he had said,

2288
01:27:22,733 --> 01:27:24,200
I'll never been
impaled on my own rack

2289
01:27:24,200 --> 01:27:25,800
this would have been ironic but.

2290
01:27:28,333 --> 01:27:31,000
(man screaming)

2291
01:27:34,467 --> 01:27:37,533
(electronic beeping)

2292
01:27:46,400 --> 01:27:47,633
(screaming)

2293
01:27:47,633 --> 01:27:49,867
- Wow, you scared me.
- What the heck are you?

2294
01:27:49,867 --> 01:27:53,000
- Look, as long as
Nelson's on the loose you

2295
01:27:53,000 --> 01:27:54,767
and I are not safe.

2296
01:27:54,767 --> 01:27:56,633
Now keep low and stick with me.

2297
01:27:56,633 --> 01:27:57,900
- What?

2298
01:27:57,900 --> 01:28:01,200
- Tom, Mike's secretly
been hunting us down.

2299
01:28:01,200 --> 01:28:02,633
Think about it.

2300
01:28:02,633 --> 01:28:04,533
He's just like the
guy in the movie.

2301
01:28:04,533 --> 01:28:07,200
All alone, isolated.

2302
01:28:07,200 --> 01:28:08,133
- Yeah.

2303
01:28:08,133 --> 01:28:10,300
- Was a sniper during the war.

2304
01:28:10,300 --> 01:28:11,233
- He was?

2305
01:28:11,233 --> 01:28:12,867
- Well I'm pretty sure, yeah.

2306
01:28:12,867 --> 01:28:14,300
- Crow, you don't think?

2307
01:28:14,300 --> 01:28:15,167
- Hi guys.

2308
01:28:15,167 --> 01:28:18,067
(screaming)

2309
01:28:18,067 --> 01:28:19,367
That was weird.

2310
01:28:19,367 --> 01:28:20,833
Well we got some letters.

2311
01:28:20,833 --> 01:28:24,167
You guys wanna join in
the letters, I guess not.

2312
01:28:24,167 --> 01:28:27,633
This first one is
from Joanne Ross.

2313
01:28:27,633 --> 01:28:29,167
I'll put that on still
story, you can see

2314
01:28:29,167 --> 01:28:30,733
the nice stickers and stuff.

2315
01:28:30,733 --> 01:28:34,233
Joanne says, dear
Mike and the robots,

2316
01:28:34,233 --> 01:28:36,867
hi, I love your show you guys
are the greatest, thanks.

2317
01:28:36,867 --> 01:28:39,200
Please do me a favor
if you get a chance,

2318
01:28:39,200 --> 01:28:41,133
would you please tell
my mom that Tom Servo

2319
01:28:41,133 --> 01:28:42,400
isn't related to ET.

2320
01:28:43,600 --> 01:28:45,800
Mom, Tom Servo is
not related to ET.

2321
01:28:45,800 --> 01:28:48,533
There's no relationship
whatsoever.

2322
01:28:48,533 --> 01:28:51,533
This next one is
from Kevin Mullins.

2323
01:28:51,533 --> 01:28:53,167
And it comes with a
nice little picture.

2324
01:28:53,167 --> 01:28:54,767
Put the letter up there.

2325
01:28:54,767 --> 01:28:57,833
It says dear Cambot
Incorporated, I would like

2326
01:28:57,833 --> 01:29:00,400
to see more Cambot on
the show, that's nice,

2327
01:29:00,400 --> 01:29:03,300
and if you say no I
will want to know why.

2328
01:29:03,300 --> 01:29:04,800
Cambot, you've been warned.

2329
01:29:04,800 --> 01:29:07,667
If Gypsy flies the ship why
doesn't she fly back to earth?

2330
01:29:09,033 --> 01:29:11,133
It's a good question, there's
no easy answers, Kevin.

2331
01:29:11,133 --> 01:29:13,133
Put that little picture
up, it's real sweet.

2332
01:29:13,133 --> 01:29:16,667
You can see, there's Crow
and there's Gypsy and Servo

2333
01:29:16,667 --> 01:29:18,500
and over here is
Boyd Gaines from

2334
01:29:18,500 --> 01:29:20,500
the old "One Day
at a Time" show.

2335
01:29:20,500 --> 01:29:23,567
So a real nice letter,
thanks Kevin and uh.

2336
01:29:23,567 --> 01:29:24,933
- [Robots] Two, one, go!

2337
01:29:24,933 --> 01:29:25,933
- Ah!

2338
01:29:25,933 --> 01:29:27,167
(chuckling)

2339
01:29:27,167 --> 01:29:28,633
Hey, what are you,
what's going on?

2340
01:29:28,633 --> 01:29:29,833
- All right, Mike.

2341
01:29:29,833 --> 01:29:31,433
We wanna hear you
promise you won't hunt

2342
01:29:31,433 --> 01:29:34,533
us down and stuff us and hang
us over the mantle piece.

2343
01:29:34,533 --> 01:29:36,967
- Well guys you know
I can't promise that.

2344
01:29:36,967 --> 01:29:38,200
(shouting)

2345
01:29:38,200 --> 01:29:40,800
Just kidding, I was
kidding you guys.

2346
01:29:40,800 --> 01:29:42,033
- Oh, I knew that.

2347
01:29:42,033 --> 01:29:43,933
- Back down to you
Dr. Florentine.

2348
01:29:43,933 --> 01:29:45,667
Come on here you little rascals.

2349
01:29:45,667 --> 01:29:47,300
- Whoa, whoa he's killing us.

2350
01:29:47,300 --> 01:29:48,233
- No I was.

2351
01:29:50,000 --> 01:29:52,167
(humming)

2352
01:29:53,367 --> 01:29:54,300
(bell chiming)

2353
01:29:54,300 --> 01:29:55,900
- Mother, dinner is ready.

2354
01:29:57,733 --> 01:29:59,400
Mom, dinner.

2355
01:29:59,400 --> 01:30:01,667
(laughing)

2356
01:30:06,100 --> 01:30:08,100
- Say Clay, nice spread.

2357
01:30:08,100 --> 01:30:09,467
What's the occasion?

2358
01:30:09,467 --> 01:30:10,800
- Don't be silly, Frank.

2359
01:30:10,800 --> 01:30:13,900
This is just our
typical evening meal.

2360
01:30:13,900 --> 01:30:15,400
Mother sit right.

2361
01:30:16,833 --> 01:30:18,600
- It looks great,
kid, it really does.

2362
01:30:18,600 --> 01:30:21,833
Don't get me wrong,
but well, Frank and I

2363
01:30:21,833 --> 01:30:23,300
are going out tonight.

2364
01:30:23,300 --> 01:30:25,700
- That's right, it's
thirsty Thursday's down

2365
01:30:25,700 --> 01:30:27,500
at the Tijuana Taxi Company.

2366
01:30:28,433 --> 01:30:30,900
(laughing)

2367
01:30:30,900 --> 01:30:33,433
- And I think I'll just stay
at the airport Ramada tonight.

2368
01:30:33,433 --> 01:30:35,067
I've got an early flight.

2369
01:30:35,067 --> 01:30:38,000
But I will see you at
the hearing, next month.

2370
01:30:39,167 --> 01:30:40,500
- Well, uh.

2371
01:30:40,500 --> 01:30:41,933
(clearing throat)

2372
01:30:41,933 --> 01:30:42,767
- Oh yes.

2373
01:30:42,767 --> 01:30:44,100
- Bye bye.

2374
01:30:44,100 --> 01:30:46,300
(giggling)

2375
01:30:56,633 --> 01:30:57,833
- Give me that!

2376
01:31:00,167 --> 01:31:02,333
(grunting)

2377
01:31:04,233 --> 01:31:06,733
(light music)

2378
01:32:06,033 --> 01:32:08,367
(screaming)

